  "### For clients",
  "Source: https://www.jamesbrady.org/work",
  "- Reminder texts for a water-filtration company (live; 2025-10 to now): A texting system driven by the company's own invoicing data. It reminds customers when a filter is due, and wins back the ones who lapsed. What it did: 207 past customers came back from January to September 2026, against about 145 in a typical year. (Method: Utlyze's published case study for a water-filtration company, comparing January to September 2026 with the same days of 2025. The company's figures as Utlyze published them; not checked from outside.) 10.6% of the customers it texted bought within 90 days, against 2.3%. (Method: Utlyze's published case study for a water-filtration company, comparing January to September 2026 with the same days of 2025. The company's figures as Utlyze published them; not checked from outside.)",
  "- A lead site for a concrete contractor (live; 2026-01-03 to now): A lead-generation website and local visibility work for a concrete contractor. What it did: The site serves on the contractor's own domain and brings in calls.",
  "- Search and AI visibility for a detox and recovery center (live; 2026-03-17 to now): Search, speed, accessibility and compliance work for a detox and recovery center. What it did: Measured gains in its Google positions, its clicks and its reviews. The figures behind those gains are not published here yet.",
  "- A new website for an HVAC company, handed over well (retired; 2026-04-03 to 2026-07): A rebuilt website and blog for a heating and cooling company. What it did: The new site brought the company leads within days. When the client left, he handed over the code, the hosting and a migration guide.",
  "- AI for a dog-breeding and kennel business (live; 2026-04 to now): A new website, visibility reports and a records portal for a dog-breeding and kennel business. What it did: AI training for the business's team. An AI system installed on the owner's own Mac, in September 2026.",
  "- An early New Reward client, a roofing company (retired; 2026-02-04 to 2026-06): Onboarding, weekly performance reports and tracing where the company's leads came from.",
  "- A lead funnel for a clean-energy tax credit (live; 2026-06-04 to 2026-06-25): A compliance-sensitive lead funnel that screens owners and investors for a clean-energy tax credit.",
  "- Advertising-compliance work for an IV-therapy clinic (live; 2026-06-16 to now): A compliance clean-up of the clinic's website: federal citations, policies rewritten in plain language, an owner-approval packet and a public task board.",
  "- A website for a dental-marketing agency (live; 2026-05-27 to 2026-07-01): The public site for an agency that sells local AI-visibility checks to dentists.",
  "- A lead site for equipment finance (live; 2026-06-29 to 2026-07-08): A fast 46-page lead-generation site, built to bring in qualified commercial-funding leads.",
  "- Visibility reports for prospective clients (shipped; 2026-07-29 to 2026-09-11): Long visibility and forensics reports for a call-center software company, a promotional-products company, a surgery center and a clinic.",
  "- Hands-on AI set-ups for trade businesses (shipped; 2026-08-21 to 2026-09-02): AI set up inside each firm, plus an executive's workstation, each aimed at the firm's real bottleneck. What it did: A construction company. A glass company. A real-estate group.",
  "- Creator campaigns for an athletic-products brand (live; 2026-09-08 to now): Influencer research and campaign management, won in about two weeks by working with the brand's own platform instead of replacing it.",
  "- An AI working session for a law firm (shipped; 2026-09-10 to 2026-09-18): An AI working brief, a two-hour session and a public guide with homework. The managing partner then agreed to an audit of the firm's systems. What it did: A two-hour working session for the firm, and a public guide with homework.",
  "- Other client and prospect work (shipped; 2025-08 to 2026-09): Smaller builds, reviews and reports for businesses in manufacturing, roofing, beauty, financial services, retail marketing, treatment, gutters and more.",
